# Python bytecode, which qtile/check.py produces every time it runs. These were
# committed once by a careless `git add -A`; the point of the file is that it
# cannot happen twice.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local overrides for one machine, kept out so that the config in git stays the
# one that describes every machine.
qtile/*_local.py

# The throwaway VM test key's public half. vm-ssh.sh serves it over HTTP to
# the guest, so the FILE has to exist in install/ while testing - but it is
# generated locally from ~/.ssh/void-vmtest and belongs to whoever is running
# the tests, not to the repository. Nothing is harmed by publishing a public
# key; it simply has no business being here.
install/vm-ssh-key.pub
